WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.211
Hackers stole photos of Uber

00:00:02.011 --> 00:00:04.706
drivers' licences without ever breaking

00:00:04.506 --> 00:00:05.293
into Uber.

00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:06.786
They came in through its

00:00:06.586 --> 00:00:07.287
AI vendor.

00:00:07.987 --> 00:00:10.115
ITPro counted at least sixteen

00:00:09.915 --> 00:00:12.340
thousand two hundred and thirty-six

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.416
affected drivers in three states.

00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:16.089
The real total is higher.

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:17.505
The haul:

00:00:17.305 --> 00:00:19.101
licence photos, names,

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.898
addresses, dates of birth and

00:00:20.698 --> 00:00:21.829
licence numbers.

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:23.171
That is most of what

00:00:22.971 --> 00:00:24.410
identity fraud needs.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.597
On October seventh,

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:29.093
attackers used valid credentials from

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:30.983
Fireworks AI, a model host.

00:00:31.023 --> 00:00:32.588
Uber's alerts were on,

00:00:32.388 --> 00:00:33.611
but nothing fired.

00:00:34.161 --> 00:00:36.187
Fireworks first said only customer

00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:37.100
secrets were read.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.123
After a second intrusion,

00:00:38.923 --> 00:00:40.976
its November update added some

00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:43.258
customers' datasets and model weights.

00:00:43.808 --> 00:00:45.236
Notion was hit too.

00:00:45.276 --> 00:00:46.934
Under one percent of its

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.195
workspaces, but the data included

00:00:48.995 --> 00:00:50.434
AI chat transcripts.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.243
Fireworks says the evidence points

00:00:53.043 --> 00:00:53.929
to an L L M

00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:54.752
jacking group.

00:00:54.792 --> 00:00:56.263
They steal AI keys,

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:57.535
sell cheap tokens,

00:00:57.335 --> 00:00:59.088
and leave victims the bill.

00:00:59.638 --> 00:01:01.155
If you use Fireworks,

00:01:00.955 --> 00:01:02.538
replace revoked keys,

00:01:02.338 --> 00:01:04.381
rotate stored secrets where they

00:01:04.181 --> 00:01:05.895
were issued, and look for

00:01:05.695 --> 00:01:07.410
anything you did not create.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.849
Everyone else should list the

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:11.741
AI vendors holding their data,

00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:12.958
and delete what no job

00:01:12.758 --> 00:01:14.918
needs, before the next bulletin.

00:01:15.468 --> 00:01:17.038
The full story has the

00:01:16.838 --> 00:01:19.323
timeline, advice for drivers,

00:01:19.123 --> 00:01:20.846
and a checklist for any

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.217
team using AI vendors.

